WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.934 --> 00:00:17.660
On the second day of the journey south, Dorothy and her friends passed through an airy forest.

2
00:00:17.661 --> 00:00:20.816
At the edge of the forest they came to a wall.

3
00:00:20.817 --> 00:00:26.337
The wall went in both directions for as far as the eye could see.

4
00:00:26.338 --> 00:00:31.988
The wall was white, shiny, and smooth, like the surface of a dish.

5
00:00:31.989 --> 00:00:34.562
It was about five meters high.

6
00:00:34.563 --> 00:00:37.564
"What shall we do now?" asked Dorothy.

7
00:00:37.565 --> 00:00:44.005
"I will make a ladder," said the Tin Man.

8
00:00:44.006 --> 00:00:47.595
The first one up the ladder was the Scarecrow.

9
00:00:47.596 --> 00:00:52.931
When the Scarecrow reached the top, he said, "Oh my! This is amazing."

10
00:00:52.932 --> 00:00:58.955
The others quickly followed him up the ladder, and all were amazed by what they saw.

11
00:00:58.956 --> 00:01:02.995
There were many brightly painted houses made of porcelain.

12
00:01:02.996 --> 00:01:08.021
Each was quite small, the biggest being only as high as Dorothy's waist.

13
00:01:08.022 --> 00:01:16.923
There were also pretty little barns with white porcelain fences and many porcelain cows, sheep, horses, pigs, and chickens.

14
00:01:16.924 --> 00:01:21.588
The porcelain people were both strange and beautiful.

15
00:01:21.589 --> 00:01:26.308
"We must cross this strange place to get to the other side," said Dorothy.

16
00:01:26.309 --> 00:01:29.940
"It would be unwise for us to go in any direction but south."

17
00:01:29.941 --> 00:01:35.848
They walked through the land, and they came to a pretty porcelain milkmaid milking a cow.

18
00:01:35.849 --> 00:01:38.317
The cow gave a sudden kick.

19
00:01:38.318 --> 00:01:42.364
The stool, the pail, and the milkmaid were knocked over.

20
00:01:42.365 --> 00:01:45.910
Dorothy was shocked to see that the cow had broken its leg.

21
00:01:45.911 --> 00:01:50.940
The milkmaid shouted at them angrily. "Look what you have done!"

22
00:01:50.941 --> 00:01:57.161
"We must be very careful," said the Tin Man. "Everything is easily broken."

23
00:01:57.162 --> 00:02:00.908
Dorothy thought all these porcelain creatures were beautiful.

24
00:02:00.909 --> 00:02:04.476
When she saw a princess, she followed her.

25
00:02:04.477 --> 00:02:08.189
The princess started to run, and Dorothy kept following.

26
00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:11.424
"Don't chase me!" yelled the princess.

27
00:02:11.425 --> 00:02:14.995
"Why not?" asked Dorothy.

28
00:02:14.996 --> 00:02:19.368
"Because if I run I might fall and break," answered the princess.

29
00:02:19.369 --> 00:02:22.546
"But you could be mended," replied Dorothy.

30
00:02:22.547 --> 00:02:27.561
"Yes, but I would not be as pretty after being mended," said the princess.

31
00:02:27.562 --> 00:02:29.542
"I think you are very beautiful.

32
00:02:29.543 --> 00:02:33.152
Will you come with me to Kansas?" asked Dorothy.

33
00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:38.369
"If I leave this land, I will turn into solid porcelain," said the princess.

34
00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:40.949
"That would make me very unhappy."

35
00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:46.692
"Oh, I didn't know," said Dorothy. "I wouldn't want that to happen."

36
00:02:46.693 --> 00:02:49.708
Dorothy and the princess waved good-bye.

37
00:02:49.709 --> 00:02:56.463
Soon the travelers came to another wall, and they climbed over it.

38
00:02:56.464 --> 00:03:01.698
"This forest is perfectly delightful," said the Lion.

39
00:03:01.699 --> 00:03:05.783
"Never have I seen a more beautiful place."

40
00:03:05.784 --> 00:03:09.029
"It seems gloomy," said the Scarecrow.

41
00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:11.885
"Not to me," replied the Lion.

42
00:03:11.886 --> 00:03:20.223
"The ground looks soft and the moss is so green, I would like to live here for the rest of my life."

43
00:03:20.224 --> 00:03:24.088
"Perhaps there are animals that live here," said Dorothy.

44
00:03:24.089 --> 00:03:29.440
"Perhaps," said the Lion. "But I do not see any of them."

45
00:03:29.441 --> 00:03:36.241
They had walked only a little farther when they came to the greatest gathering of wild beasts they had ever seen.

46
00:03:36.242 --> 00:03:40.670
"Welcome, King of the Beasts," said a tiger.

47
00:03:40.671 --> 00:03:44.271
"Have you come to fight the monster?"

48
00:03:44.272 --> 00:03:47.322
"What monster?" asked the Lion.

49
00:03:47.323 --> 00:03:52.757
The tiger described a spider-like creature as large as an elephant.

50
00:03:52.758 --> 00:03:58.336
The Lion thought for a moment and asked, "Are there any other lions in this forest?"

51
00:03:58.337 --> 00:04:04.545
"Not now," answered the tiger. "The monster has eaten them."

52
00:04:04.546 --> 00:04:12.418
"If I kill this monster for you, will you bow before me and call me your king?" asked the Lion.

53
00:04:12.419 --> 00:04:17.176
"We will!" roared all the animals at once.

54
00:04:17.177 --> 00:04:23.339
The monster was sleeping when the Lion found it, and it was as ugly as the tiger had described.

55
00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:25.510
The Lion saw the monster's weakness.

56
00:04:25.511 --> 00:04:31.071
It had a large head that was connected to a large body by a slender neck.

57
00:04:31.072 --> 00:04:41.699
The Lion jumped, landed on the monster's back, and used his large paw to knock the monster's head from its body.

58
00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:45.992
The Lion returned, and the animals gave a great cheer.

59
00:04:45.993 --> 00:04:50.036
"I have killed the monster," the Lion declared.

60
00:04:50.037 --> 00:04:53.261
All the animals bowed before their new king.

61
00:04:53.262 --> 00:04:57.988
"Now I must help Dorothy return to Kansas," said the Lion.

62
00:04:57.989 --> 00:05:04.457
"After that I will return."
